<p>Before you continue: this installation stores your bookkeeping data — accounts, transactions,
receipts, and any personal data of other people that passes through them.</p>

<h2>Who can see it</h2>

<p>The administrators of this installation with top-level access can open any set of books on it,
including yours. That is inherent to how self-hosting works, not a choice this particular
installation makes: whoever runs the server is always the one person for whom there is no
technical way to keep the data private.</p>

<h2>Your own account</h2>

<p>Your username, email address, and a record of your sign-ins — including failed ones — are kept
for security. That stays on this installation; it is not shared anywhere else.</p>

<h2>How long records are kept</h2>

<p>Bookkeeping records are kept for as long as your access is active, and afterwards for as long as
the law that applies to your business requires — then deleted. See
<%= link_to "the full privacy notice", legal_url %> for the detail.</p>

<p>This is a short summary of how this installation handles your data, not a full legal contract.
Agreeing confirms you were told this before you continued.</p>
